# i18n — English-only for new entries

When adding or updating keys in `packages/ledger-button/src/i18n/`, **always use English** for new string values. Do not translate new copy into French, German, Spanish, or any other locale.

## Rules

- Add new keys to **every** locale file (`en.json`, `fr.json`, `de.json`, etc.) so structure stays in sync.
- Use the **same English text** in all locale files for new entries. Existing translated strings in non-`en` files must not be changed unless explicitly asked.
- Preserve placeholders and ICU-style tokens exactly (e.g. `{count}`, `{name}`).
- Product names and brand terms stay as in source (e.g. `Ledger`, `Ledger Wallet`).

## Examples

```json
// ✅ GOOD — new key added everywhere in English
// en.json, fr.json, de.json, ...
"accountTokens": {
  "emptyState": "No tokens found for this account"
}

// ❌ BAD — translating while adding the key
// fr.json
"emptyState": "Aucun jeton trouvé pour ce compte"

// ❌ BAD — English only in en.json, missing keys in other locales
```

Professional translation of non-English locales is handled separately; your job is keys + English copy only.
